cifs: change tcon status when need_reconnect is set on it

jira KERNEL-814
Rebuild_History Non-Buildable kernel-4.18.0-553.115.1.el8_10
commit-author Shyam Prasad N <sprasad@microsoft.com>
commit c6e02eefd6ace3da3369c764f15429f5647056af
Empty-Commit: Cherry-Pick Conflicts during history rebuild.
Will be included in final tarball splat. Ref for failed cherry-pick at:
ciq/ciq_backports/kernel-4.18.0-553.115.1.el8_10/c6e02eef.failed

When a tcon is marked for need_reconnect, the intention
is to have it reconnected.

This change adjusts tcon->status in cifs_tree_connect
when need_reconnect is set. Also, this change has a minor
correction in resetting need_reconnect on success. It makes
sure that it is done with tc_lock held.

	Signed-off-by: Shyam Prasad N <sprasad@microsoft.com>
	Signed-off-by: Steve French <stfrench@microsoft.com>
(cherry picked from commit c6e02eefd6ace3da3369c764f15429f5647056af)
	Signed-off-by: Jonathan Maple <jmaple@ciq.com>

